; Minimal reproduction, found while building K0 (2026-11-01):
; the v1.1 surface parser cannot resolve a call to a function
; defined LATER in the module. This four-line program makes
; krellc exit with a segmentation fault instead of a parse
; result. K0 sources work around it by declaring callees
; before their callers (gen_kernel.py output is written in
; dependency order). A fix belongs in src/surface.c: pass 1
; must register every function shell before any body is parsed.
fn b() -> void {
  entry():
    call void a()
    ret
}
fn a() -> void {
  entry():
    ret
}
